    description: "Source: DEEP cohort 1 reflect on deep-20260510-054430 (apollo-server, nestjs, chatwoot reflect agents). Sample stats: apollo-server 0/80 calls edges carry access_mode != 'none'; nestjs 0/61. By contrast Go and Python sit at roughly 50-60% coverage. Field is uniformly 'none' on TypeScript and JavaScript output, which makes the --dataflow slice flag useless on the language stack that dominates the prospector corpus. Related background invariant INV-jahov-minur-bogul-mijul-kutig-viral-potil-kuviv (satisfied) requires the read/write distinction to be carried; this finding is that the TS/JS analyzers don't classify at all (the 'none' default propagates everywhere). Fix direction: implement parameter-flow access_mode classification in the TS/JS analyzer for primitives like assignment, augmented assignment, .push/.pop/.shift, get/set property accessors. Evidence files: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/deep-20260510-054430/reflect/cohort-001/iter-001/{apollo-server,nestjs,chatwoot}.assessment.yaml."  # 130e
    fields: {}  # 130e
